<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1246" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδημονέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be sorely troubled</i> or <i>dismayed, be in anguish,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Virg.</u>
				1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδημονῶν τε καὶ ἀπορῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					175d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				19.197
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδημονῆσαι τὰς ψυχάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					4.4.3
				</span></i>
			: c. dat. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδημονεῖ τᾗ ἀτοπίᾳ τοῦ πάθους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					251d
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπό τινος</span>
			<i>to be puzzled</i> by . ., <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Nat.</u>
				11.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					3.70
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάριν τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					298.45
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>. (<i><span class="en">Eust.,
			833.15</span></i>, derives it from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδήμων</span>, which is found only as
				v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				1.18
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>).<i><span class="en">
				177
			</span></i>), and is itself of doubtful derivation.) [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰδ-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			.]</div>
